hi,

i have grated 3 patches for gnomehack. descriptions as follows:

1. gnome-config.diff

this patch changes the GNOMEINC and the WINGNOMELIB contents to use the
gnome-config function, ensuring that the correct location of the libs will
always be found.

2. gnome-rawprint.diff

the gnome port was using tty_raw_print instead of just raw_print.

3. gnome-tiles.diff

a) this diff fixes a few problems. the first one begin that HACKDIR was used
within the code at compile-time as the *exclusive* location for data, not
allowing for setting of the HACKDIR environment variable. it would crash if
the tiles/dat directory were located elsewhere

b) when tilesets changed, the screen didn't actually refresh, this is due to
the port calling "doredraw()" and, NetHack itself does not refresh if it is
currently waiting for a keypress (perhaps this could be addressed withing
NetHack somehow ?). I fixed this by passing a [C-r] instead of calling
"doredraw", this does not always work either, eg if the player is within some
menu, but it does work more often, and most players in my opinion would
change the tileset once at the game start, once they've found their favorite,
so most will never notice when it does fail.

c) origionally the code catered for 2 tilesets, namely the traditional, and
itakura's tileset which it wanted as "t32-1024.xpm".  i changed it to expect
2"itakura.xpm" instead, added support for the following other tilesets :
"absurd", "abigaba", "geoduck", "lagged", and one miscelanious use set i
called "other".

d) the port would origionally crash if a tileset that didn't exist on the
users drive was selected.  now it only displays for selection those already
installed.


all patches as well as additional tilesets, and a "for linux" patch can be
downloaded from:

http://www.linuxgames.co.za/NetHack/ports/gnome/


